# link-local-packages

This rule is a discovery wrapper, not a second implementation.

Read and follow the canonical [link-local-packages skill](../../.claude/skills/link-local-packages/SKILL.md) completely before acting. Resolve every helper and resource from that canonical skill directory; this wrapper intentionally contains no duplicated scripts.

Key constraints, repeated here so they are visible before the canonical file is opened:

- Invoke the bundled helper only; do not improvise `npm link`, `ln -s`, or `file:` dependency edits.
- Never link across contexts — reference clones under `repos/` and feature worktrees under `specs/<spec-name>/repos/` must not be mixed.
- `npm install` and `npm ci` in a consumer silently remove links.
